                <pb facs="1179" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1063"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.00/129.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister McMillin to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram February 12. I today answered the note of Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs. A majority of the countries represented here have taken similar action,
                    and others will now. French Minister had determined to act with the United
                    States. China and Colombia manifested same intention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
